{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:InformationTheory.HopfLinkSymmetricDecomposition","@type":"LeanModule","name":"InformationTheory.HopfLinkSymmetricDecomposition","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Units","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HopfSymmetric.hopf_symmetric_decomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HopfSymmetric.hopf_symmetric_decomposition","kind":"theorem","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/hopf-link-symmetric-decomposition.lean#L40-L54","doc":"**Hopf-link symmetric/antisymmetric decomposition.**\n\nGiven the 2-strand Hecke relation `σ² = (q − q⁻¹)·σ + 1`, the Hopf element\n`σ²` decomposes over the two block projectors `(σ + q⁻¹)` and `(q − σ)`\nwith weights `q²` and `q⁻²` (the squared block eigenvalues), after clearing\nthe `[2]_q = q + q⁻¹` denominator. Sorry-free. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:hopf-link-symmetric-decomposition","label":"prop:hopf-link-symmetric-decomposition","md":"quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/hopf-link-symmetric-decomposition.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}